# AI Handoff — data/

**Updated:** 2026-09-18  
**Scope:** source data, external covariates, geospatial joins, feature construction and data QA.

For full project context read `docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md` and `docs/PROJECT_HISTORY.md` first.

## Core supervised contract

```text
ID_POLIGONO
RENDIMIENTO_T_HA
CONJUNTO
197 parcels
138 ENTRENAMIENTO
59 PREDICCION
target cycle: April–October 2025
states: Hidalgo, Puebla, Tlaxcala
```

The supervised unit is the parcel. BASIC/PRO rows are repeated parcel/date/sensor observations,
not independent target samples.

Never use hidden prediction targets.

## Official sources

### Split

`data/source/tabular/ID_area_rendimiento_70_30_Reto_AgroCebada.csv`

Defines the 197 parcel IDs, official split, area and target availability.

### Parcels

`data/source/geospatial/Parcelas_Reto_AGC_CONJUNTO_70_30.zip`

Observed CRS: EPSG:4326.

Canonical loader normalization:

```text
ID_POLIGON -> ID_POLIGONO
área_ha    -> area_ha
```

### BASIC

```text
107,666 rows × 96 columns
197 parcels
2022–2025
Sentinel-2 + Landsat
23 index families × promedio/std/max/min
```

Dates are day-first. Preserve sensor provenance. Missingness is sensor-specific.

### PRO

```text
47,804 rows × 20 columns
197 parcels
2025
Planet
NDVI/EVI/LAI/MSAVI × promedio/std/max/min
```

Do not silently merge same-named indices across Sentinel/Landsat/Planet.

### Official climate/topography

Official monthly precipitation and Tmin/Tmax cover 2022–2025.

Official topography contains elevation/slope products. See `docs/DATA_SOURCES.md` for current
CRS/resolution details.

## External local data

Large external downloads remain local under `data/raw/external/` and are not committed.

Data Contract v2 certified the prioritized external set:

- INEGI municipal boundaries for Hidalgo/Puebla/Tlaxcala;
- CHIRPS daily 2025-04-01 through 2025-10-31, 214 files;
- WaPOR AETI and NPP, 21 dekads each;
- SoilGrids: 9 properties × 4 depths = 36 rasters;
- SIAP: every year 2003–2025;
- high-resolution INEGI CEM for the three target states.

ERA5-Land is intentionally optional and is not a completeness requirement.

## Join/data policies

Administrative/SIAP joins use official parcel Estado/Municipio as primary.

INEGI municipality overlap is QA/fallback, not silent replacement.

Use full SIAP CVEGEO:

```text
zfill(Idestado, 2) + zfill(Idmunicipio, 3)
```

Never join on municipality ID alone.

Keep `Cebada grano` separate from forage barley.

SIAP 2025 is competition-only because it is contemporaneous municipal outcome information.

SoilGrids unit/scale conversion and source-specific CRS handling are frozen in
`configs/data_contract_v2.yaml`.

WaPOR seasonal totals use band duration metadata; do not simply sum rate values.

## Data Contract v2

Run:

```powershell
python tools\audit_data_contract_v2.py
```

Latest full-workstation result:

```text
PASS 46
WARN 0
FAIL 0
SKIP 1
```

The SKIP is intentional ERA5-Land policy.

If source/raw data change, rerun the contract before regenerating model-ready artifacts.

## Integration fixtures

The shared 12-parcel integration fixtures are complete and validated.

They exercise official/external joins and raster/NetCDF extraction on a small real subset.

Builder:

```powershell
python tools\build_integration_fixtures.py
```

Do not redesign fixture selection unless the contract changes.

