Canonical directory:

```text
data/processed/features_v1/
```

Artifacts:

```text
parcel_features_clean.csv
parcel_features_competition.csv
parcel_features_all.csv
feature_manifest.json
build_report.json
README.md
```

Validated shapes:

```text
clean        197 × 699
competition  197 × 1408
all          197 × 1408
```

Manifest:

```text
694 clean features
709 competition-only features
1403 total features
1401 numeric
```

All 138 training targets are present. All 59 prediction targets are missing.

Use `feature_manifest.json` for feature provenance/mode instead of guessing from names.

## Feature namespaces

Expected namespaces include:

```text
base_*
admin_*
sat_basic_*
sat_pro_*
clim_official_*
chirps_daily_*
wapor_*
soilgrids_*
topo_official_*
cem15_*
siap_hist_*
siap_2025_*
```

## Clean vs competition

`clean`
: historical/static representation.

`competition`
: clean plus rule-permitted 2025/full-season/contemporaneous public information.

Do not collapse this distinction.

The exact operational forecast cutoff is still unresolved.

## Current QC caveats

Only one CHIRPS daily competition feature survives Feature Table v1. Most candidate CHIRPS
daily aggregate features were dropped as all-null. Investigate before relying on CHIRPS.

The feature builder emitted pandas fragmentation warnings during daily CHIRPS construction;
this is a performance issue, not a failed build.

The workstation also reported an h5py/HDF5 build/runtime mismatch warning during WaPOR work;
WaPOR extraction nevertheless completed.

## Git policy

Versioned:

- official source evidence;
- integration fixtures;
- canonical `data/processed/features_v1/`;
- manifests/contracts/reports.

Not versioned:

- large raw external downloads;
- transient interim outputs;
- arbitrary processed experiments.

Do not remove local raw data merely to make Git clean.

## Non-negotiable guards

- preserve `ID_POLIGONO`;
- no many-to-many accidental joins;
- no row-random supervised split of BASIC/PRO;
- no hidden-target use;
- preserve sensor provenance;
- explicit CRS handling;
- no guessed units/formulas;
- learned preprocessing fitted inside CV folds;
- source files remain immutable.

For the full rationale, read `docs/DATA_SOURCES.md`, `docs/DATA_CONTRACT_V2.md`,
`docs/FEATURE_TABLE_V1.md` and `checkpoints/01_data/README.md`.
